{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue\/threequartersflat"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO17threeQuartersFlatyA2CmF","title":"MXLAccidentalValue.threeQuartersFlat","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"threeQuartersFlat"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Tartini-style three-quarter-tone flat accidental."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/threeQuartersFlat"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"threeQuartersFlat"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue/threeQuartersFlat":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAccidentalValue.threeQuartersFlat","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue\/threequartersflat","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Tartini-style three-quarter-tone flat accidental."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/threeQuartersFlat","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"threeQuartersFlat"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"title":"MXLAccidentalValue","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}